* Hyperliquid\nby theme
** Chain and execution
*** HyperBFT\n//consensus over block contents and order//
*** HyperCore\n//the exchange half of the state//
*** HyperEVM\n//the general-purpose contract half//
*** Dual-block architecture\n//two interleaved EVM block types//
*** Intra-block action ordering\n//the sequence of actions in a block//
*** L1Read precompiles\n//contracts read HyperCore state//
*** CoreWriter\n//contracts write to HyperCore//
** Actors and access
*** Validator\n//stakes, builds blocks, publishes prices//
*** Maker and taker\n//the two roles in any trade//
*** API wallet and the nonce set\n//delegated key, master key stays cold//
*** Slashing surface\n//staked HYPE burnable by vote//
** The instrument and the book
*** Perpetual future (perp)\n//no expiry, no delivery//
*** Central limit order book (CLOB)\n//resting orders by price then time//
*** HYPE\n//the chain's native token//
** Prices
*** Oracle price\n//validator reference, every few seconds//
*** Mark price\n//values positions and triggers events//
*** Funding rate\n//holds the perp near the underlying//
left side
** Margin and account state
*** Clearinghouse\n//owns positions and collateral//
*** Margin\n//collateral backing a position//
*** Cross margin and isolated margin\n//shared or ring-fenced collateral//
*** Maintenance margin\n//floor before liquidation//
*** Margin tier\n//size bracket setting that floor//
*** Portfolio margin\n//one collateral pool, many positions//
** When a position fails
*** Liquidation\n//forced close below maintenance//
*** Auto-deleveraging (ADL)\n//last rung once equity goes negative//
*** HLP (Hyperliquidity Provider)\n//community vault taking the backstop//
** Deployable primitives
*** HIP-1 (native token standard)\n//token plus its spot book//
*** HIP-2 (Hyperliquidity)\n//operator-free market-making ladder//
*** HIP-3 (builder-deployed perpetuals)\n//permissionless perp DEX//
*** HIP-4 (outcome market)\n//fully collateralised, bounded range//
@endmindmap
